<h1 id=3D"FeatureManagement-ArchitectureAssessments">Architecture Assessmen=
ts</h1>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"relative-table wrapped confluenceTable" style=3D"width: 83=
.2691%;">
  <colgroup>
   <col style=3D"width: 6.94291%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 66.9165%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 26.1107%;">
  </colgroup>
  <tbody>
   <tr>
    <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Assessment No.</th>
    <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Description</th>
    <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Implications</th>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">AA.001</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"7906da5e-b057-4a=
87-8b93-ddda36e1bd4f">Okta doesn't have a constraint preventing multi </spa=
n><em><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"7906da5e-b057-4a87-=
8b93-ddda36e1bd4f">user-group</span></em><span class=3D"inline-comment-mark=
er" data-ref=3D"7906da5e-b057-4a87-8b93-ddda36e1bd4f"> support. Instead, it=
 follows the following security principle</span>s:</p>
      <ul>
       <li><em>Scopes</em> are unique to <em>rules</em>
        <ul>
         <li>In other words, a <em>scope</em> must not be shared across <em=
>rules</em>. Each <em>rule</em> has a unique set of <em>scopes</em>.</li>
        </ul></li>
       <li><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"68dcaba2-eb70-=
48f4-9323-e5a9eab4c01a">A&nbsp;</span><em><span class=3D"inline-comment-mar=
ker" data-ref=3D"68dcaba2-eb70-48f4-9323-e5a9eab4c01a">user</span></em><spa=
n class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"68dcaba2-eb70-48f4-9323-e5a9e=
ab4c01a"> can play&nbsp;</span><strong><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker=
" data-ref=3D"68dcaba2-eb70-48f4-9323-e5a9eab4c01a">one and only one </span=
></strong><em><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"68dcaba2-eb=
70-48f4-9323-e5a9eab4c01a">role</span></em><strong><span class=3D"inline-co=
mment-marker" data-ref=3D"68dcaba2-eb70-48f4-9323-e5a9eab4c01a"> </span><u>=
<span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"68dcaba2-eb70-48f4-9323-e=
5a9eab4c01a">at a time</span></u></strong>
        <ul>
         <li>In other words, a&nbsp;<em>user</em> cannot ask for a <em>toke=
n</em> with a set of <em>scopes (permissions)</em> spanned across several <=
em>rules (roles)</em>. <span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"10=
8bd041-c263-4ade-b81c-e63a8fcc3fa0">It can only ask for a </span><em><span =
class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"108bd041-c263-4ade-b81c-e63a8fc=
c3fa0">token</span></em><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"1=
08bd041-c263-4ade-b81c-e63a8fcc3fa0"> with a set of </span><em><span class=
=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"108bd041-c263-4ade-b81c-e63a8fcc3fa0=
">scopes</span></em><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"108bd=
041-c263-4ade-b81c-e63a8fcc3fa0"> specific to a single </span><em><span cla=
ss=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"108bd041-c263-4ade-b81c-e63a8fcc3f=
a0">rule</span></em>. In addition, the <em>user</em> must be a member of th=
e referenced&nbsp;<em>user-group</em> of that&nbsp;<em>rule</em>.</li>
        </ul></li>
      </ul>
      <p><img class=3D"drawio-diagram-image" width=3D"468" style=3D"width:5=
31px;max-width: 100%;" src=3D"7d21a7e1804ef758036f8b4244fac24a1e740cc6df008=
1081322acc1ed9d1272" height=3D"313"></p>
     </div></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">A <em>user</em> can be a member of multiple =
<em>user-groups</em>, but it can only ask for a <em>token</em> with a set o=
f <em>scopes</em> part of a single <em>rule</em>.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">AA.002</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p><em>Package templates</em> are the authoritative source of truth of=
 <em>package assignments</em>. It specifies the following:</p>
     <ul>
      <li><em>Resources</em> contained in the <em>package</em></li>
      <li><em><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"41811307-d5=
53-4557-9f23-018846349ee7">Permissions</span></em><span class=3D"inline-com=
ment-marker" data-ref=3D"41811307-d553-4557-9f23-018846349ee7"> required fo=
r consuming these </span><em><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=
=3D"41811307-d553-4557-9f23-018846349ee7">resources</span></em></li>
     </ul></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Assigning a <em>package</em> to a <em>user</em> assigns, by default=
, the <em>package</em>'s <em>user-group</em>&nbsp;to the <em>user</em>. But=
 when requesting a <em>token</em> for consuming the <em>package</em>'s<em> =
resources</em>, the set of <em>scopes</em> (<em>permissions</em>) required =
should be retrieved from the&nbsp;<em>user</em> <em>package assignment</em>=
&nbsp;and not from the <em>user-group assignment</em>, all the more to enab=
le <em>multi-user-group assignments</em>.</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p>AA.003</p>
      <p><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"FeatureManagement-AA.=
003"></span></p>
     </div></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"57b89fc0-62a6-4d=
50-8097-3b360874cb18">Adding/removing a </span><em><span class=3D"inline-co=
mment-marker" data-ref=3D"57b89fc0-62a6-4d50-8097-3b360874cb18">feature</sp=
an></em><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"57b89fc0-62a6-4d5=
0-8097-3b360874cb18"> to a </span><em><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker"=
 data-ref=3D"57b89fc0-62a6-4d50-8097-3b360874cb18">user template</span></em=
><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"57b89fc0-62a6-4d50-8097-=
3b360874cb18">, implies the following</span>:</p>
      <ol>
       <li>Add/remove the <em>resource</em>&nbsp;to the <em>user </em><em>t=
emplate</em></li>
       <li><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"e91971f4-2b34-=
4410-85e4-079d3f68496d">Update the </span><em><span class=3D"inline-comment=
-marker" data-ref=3D"e91971f4-2b34-4410-85e4-079d3f68496d">user-group </spa=
n></em><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"e91971f4-2b34-4410=
-85e4-079d3f68496d">of&nbsp;the </span><em><span class=3D"inline-comment-ma=
rker" data-ref=3D"e91971f4-2b34-4410-85e4-079d3f68496d">user </span></em><e=
m><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"e91971f4-2b34-4410-85e4=
-079d3f68496d">template</span></em>
        <ul>
         <li>Add/remove the required <em>permission</em> to/from an existin=
g <em>role</em> referenced by the <em>user-group</em> OR</li>
         <li><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"21cea1c5-f9a=
2-4f39-8611-64427c331f5c">Create a new </span><em><span class=3D"inline-com=
ment-marker" data-ref=3D"21cea1c5-f9a2-4f39-8611-64427c331f5c">role</span><=
/em><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"21cea1c5-f9a2-4f39-86=
11-64427c331f5c">, add the required </span><em><span class=3D"inline-commen=
t-marker" data-ref=3D"21cea1c5-f9a2-4f39-8611-64427c331f5c">permission</spa=
n></em><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"21cea1c5-f9a2-4f39=
-8611-64427c331f5c"> to the </span><em><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker=
" data-ref=3D"21cea1c5-f9a2-4f39-8611-64427c331f5c">role</span></em><span c=
lass=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"21cea1c5-f9a2-4f39-8611-64427c33=
1f5c"> and the </span><em><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D=
"21cea1c5-f9a2-4f39-8611-64427c331f5c">role</span></em><span class=3D"inlin=
e-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"21cea1c5-f9a2-4f39-8611-64427c331f5c"> to the=
 </span><em><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"21cea1c5-f9a2=
-4f39-8611-64427c331f5c">user-group</span>&nbsp;</em></li>
        </ul></li>
       <li>Update <em>user packages</em>
        <ul>
         <li>Find all&nbsp;<em>user packages</em> referencing the <em>user =
</em><em>template</em>
          <ul>
           <li>For each, add/remove the&nbsp;<em>feature</em> to/from the <=
em>user package</em></li>
          </ul></li>
        </ul></li>
       <li>Update <em>user assignments</em>
        <ul>
         <li>Find every <em>user assignment</em>&nbsp;referencing the <em>u=
ser packages</em>
          <ul>
           <li>For each, create/delete a/the <em>resource assignment</em>
            <ul>
             <li>Assign/unassign the&nbsp;<em>resource</em> to the referenc=
ed <em>user</em></li>
            </ul></li>
           <li><strong>N.B. </strong>No change is required to the&nbsp;<em>=
package assignments</em> neither to the <em>user-group assignments</em></li=
>
          </ul></li>
        </ul></li>
       <li>Update <em>firm assignments</em>
        <ul>
         <li>For each <em>user</em>, find their <em>firm</em>
          <ul>
           <li>For each firm, find their package assignment=20
            <ul>
             <li>For each <em>package assignment</em>, update the <em>firm =
package</em>
              <ul>
               <li>Add/remove the <em>feature</em> to/from the underlying <=
em>firm template</em>
                <ul>
                 <li>Add/remove the&nbsp;<em>resource</em> to/from the <em>=
firm </em><em>template</em></li>
                </ul></li>
               <li>Add/remove the <em>feature</em> to/from the&nbsp;<em>fir=
m package</em></li>
              </ul></li>
            </ul></li>
          </ul></li>
        </ul></li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>N.B.</strong>&nbsp;<em>Scopes</em> don't translate into <e=
m>permissions</em> in Compass X (as done elsewhere) but to <em>roles</em>. =
Therefore, <em>rules</em> defined in Okta for Compass X contain both <em>pe=
rmissions</em> (e.g. For SOM-A accesses) and <em>roles</em> (for Compass X =
accesses), which leads to confusion as in the example below with ManageTrad=
e <em>rule</em>.</p>
      <div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
       <div class=3D"codeHeader panelHeader pdl" style=3D"border-bottom-wid=
th: 1px;">
        <b>ManageTrade rule</b>
       </div>
       <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
        <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=
=3D"brush: java; gutter: true">--User Group--
Wealth.CompassX.ManageTrade

--SOM-A scopes (as permissions)--
wealth:rrsp-withdrawal-eligible-positions:read,=20
wealth:rrsp-withdrawal:read,=20
wealth:tfsa-withdrawal-eligible-positions:read,=20
wealth:tfsa-withdrawal:read,=20
...

--Compass X scopes (as roles)--
wealth:aom:accountbasicviewer,=20
wealth:aom:accountportfolioviewer,=20
wealth:aom:viewer,=20
wealth:moe:viewer,
...</pre>
       </div>
      </div>
      <p>Ref.</p>
      <ul>
       <li><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://auth0.com/docs/get-st=
arted/apis/scopes" rel=3D"nofollow">Scopes (auth0.com)</a></li>
       <li><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://www.oauth.com/oauth2-=
servers/scope/" rel=3D"nofollow">Scope - OAuth 2.0 Simplified</a>
        <ul>
         <li><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://www.oauth.com/oauth=
2-servers/scope/defining-scopes/" rel=3D"nofollow">Defining Scopes - OAuth =
2.0 Simplified</a></li>
        </ul></li>
      </ul>
     </div></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p>The steps can be automated to enable the <em>feature package</em> =
update. But as stated by&nbsp;<a class=3D"confluence-userlink user-mention"=
 data-username=3D"rava001" href=3D"/display/~rava001" data-linked-resource-=
id=3D"994246714" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-ty=
pe=3D"userinfo" data-base-url=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca">Anand Raveendran</a> =
, updating dynamically <em>user-groups</em> (i.e. <em>roles</em> &amp; <em>=
permissions</em>) in Compass X would require to also update&nbsp;<em>rules<=
/em> dynamically in Okta to add/remove&nbsp;<em>scopes</em>. Unfortunately,=
 that capability is not available.&nbsp;</p>
      <p>As we need more flexibility, Okta could be limited to handle coars=
e-grained access control. For instance, Okta would grant access to modules =
or resource groups, and Compass X would control the access to resources.</p=
>
      <p>Another option is to limit <em>package</em> updates to <em>resourc=
es</em> with <em>permissions</em> already/to-be assigned to the current <em=
>roles</em> of the <em>user-group</em>. (p.s. Assigning new <em>permissions=
</em> would be on the condition they are from the same <em>capability</em> =
as the <em>role</em>).&nbsp;As noted, <strong>Okta <u><em>scopes</em></u> a=
re translated to&nbsp;<u><em>roles</em></u> in Compass X</strong>. So by no=
t updating the&nbsp;predefined list of&nbsp;<em>roles</em>, no new <em>role=
s</em> would be created in Compass X, and therefore no new&nbsp;<em>scopes<=
/em> would need to be added to the <em>rule</em> in Okta, hence no syncing =
needed with Okta.</p>
     </div></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">AA.004</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p>By definition:</p>
      <ul>
       <li>A <em>user-group</em> is a grouping of <em>users</em> playing on=
e or several <em>roles</em></li>
      </ul>
      <p>That concept of <em>user-group</em> is applied loosely in Compass =
X, e.g.:</p>
      <ul>
       <li>When referenced by a <em style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">templa=
te</em><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">, it serves solely as securit=
y specifications (i.e. set of&nbsp;</span><em style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0p=
x;">permissions</em><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;"> required to con=
sume its </span><em style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">resources</em><span st=
yle=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">). </span></li>
       <li>When assigned to a&nbsp;<em style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">use=
r</em><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">, it acts as a typical </span>=
<em style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">user-group</em><span style=3D"letter-s=
pacing: 0.0px;"> with a set of </span><em style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">=
permissions</em><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">.</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p>Moreover, the concept of <em>permission</em> is confused with the =
one of <em>role</em>. By definition:</p>
      <ul>
       <li>A <em>permission</em> is an approval of a mode of access to a <e=
m>resource</em> (e.g. Read)</li>
       <li>A <em>role</em> is a job function or title which defines an auth=
ority level (e.g. Reader)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Ref. <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w=
iki/Role-based_access_control" rel=3D"nofollow">Role-based access control -=
 Wikipedia</a></p>
      <p>That being said, in the data model, there is no relationship (dire=
ct/indirect) between a <em>permission</em> and the specific <em>resource</e=
m> it controls, but it is implied (in the <em>permission</em> name).</p>
      <p><img class=3D"drawio-diagram-image" width=3D"468" style=3D"width:9=
81px;max-width: 100%;" src=3D"818257abe052c7b1b7e63c4137c1a7815e272a1b1b13a=
6615adaadf2dc9b427c" height=3D"114"></p>
      <p>The sole purpose of a <em>user template</em> is to specify a set o=
f <em>permissions</em> for a group of <em>resources </em>assignable to <em>=
users</em> (p.s. in comparison to <em>firm template</em>, which sole purpos=
e is to group <em>resources</em> assignable to <em>firms</em>).</p>
      <p>The main purpose of a <em>user package</em> is to specify the set =
of <em>permissions</em> a <em>user</em> needs when assigned a group of <em>=
resources</em>.</p>
     </div></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p>The concept of <em>user template</em> and <em>user package</em> co=
uld be removed altogether. Their purpose could be met with the proper appli=
cation of RBAC underneath the concept of <em>feature package</em>.</p>
      <p><span style=3D"color:#164555;"><img class=3D"drawio-diagram-image"=
 width=3D"468" style=3D"width:891px;max-width: 100%;" src=3D"c22472e78d2804=
66b02d837f2a64157709dd0e143822eb5f41531520e6f65125" height=3D"268"></span><=
/p>
     </div></td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
